WEBVTT

00:00:00.850 --> 00:00:05.750
You Show School is dueling LDS in a 
best-of-three match with our school on the line.

00:00:06.690 --> 00:00:11.420
Yuya defeated the Xyz user Hokuto 
Shijima for the first win.

00:00:11.600 --> 00:00:13.500
It gave me shivers!

00:00:13.500 --> 00:00:19.150
But Yuzu lost against the 
Fusion user Masumi Koutsu.

00:00:19.150 --> 00:00:25.250
It was unfortunate, but that Fusion user 
was so beautiful that she gave me shivers!

00:00:26.300 --> 00:00:33.150
With one win and one loss, Gongenzaka is dueling 
the Synchro user Yaiba Toudou in the third match.

00:00:33.150 --> 00:00:35.850
He Synchro Summoned twice in a row!

00:00:35.850 --> 00:00:40.450
He already summoned two powerful 
monsters!  Gongenzaka, will you be okay?

00:00:40.650 --> 00:00:42.620
It's. Mr. Gongenzaka!

00:00:42.620 --> 00:00:46.390
How dare you forget the “Mr.” part!

00:00:46.390 --> 00:00:48.000
Don't worry.

00:00:48.000 --> 00:00:55.300
The man Gongenzaka promises to win for his 
friend Yuya and protect You Show School!

00:00:56.600 --> 00:01:02.240
Implementing mass into Solid 
Vision has created Action Duels.

00:01:02.370 --> 00:01:10.620
In duels where the field, monsters and duelists 
become one, the people are caught in a frenzy of excitement!

00:01:11.800 --> 00:01:14.420
Believe x Believe  Biri-Biri-Biri Buddies!

00:01:30.110 --> 00:01:33.200
You!  The strongest card 
isn't about winning or losing

00:01:33.520 --> 00:01:36.610
You!  At full speed  On the game

00:01:43.670 --> 00:01:45.350
Swinging ma ma ma mind

00:01:45.350 --> 00:01:49.920
The soul's pendulum  Ultimate confusion

00:01:50.470 --> 00:01:52.120
Impulse  Got it got it

00:01:52.120 --> 00:01:57.330
Tough battles  Real revolution

00:02:03.690 --> 00:02:08.090
Everybody goin'  Break through the walls!

00:02:10.310 --> 00:02:15.010
Infinite future  Get rid of indecision!

00:02:15.700 --> 00:02:18.950
Make it Make it  Be courageous (Break it now)

00:02:18.950 --> 00:02:22.350
Step ahead!  Take a step (Do it now)

00:02:22.350 --> 00:02:32.630
The fun is only getting started!  
So everyone's a Believer!!

00:02:32.950 --> 00:02:35.970
Believe x Believe  Biri-Biri-Biri Buddies!

00:02:40.020 --> 00:02:46.030
Body and Sword as One!!  
Synchro User Yaiba Toudou

00:03:06.400 --> 00:03:08.190
He's incredible.

00:03:08.190 --> 00:03:11.500
He Synchro Summoned twice in one turn.

00:03:14.470 --> 00:03:16.090
What's wrong?

00:03:16.090 --> 00:03:18.290
Are you so shocked that you can't speak?

00:03:18.290 --> 00:03:22.390
A man stands firm and doesn't get flustered.

00:03:22.390 --> 00:03:26.220
You cannot win by running around!

00:03:26.220 --> 00:03:28.090
Like you know!

00:03:28.090 --> 00:03:30.190
I'll show you no mercy!

00:03:30.190 --> 00:03:31.540
Let's battle!

00:03:31.540 --> 00:03:36.460
XX-Saber Gottoms attacks 
Superheavy Samurai Kabuto!

00:03:41.670 --> 00:03:45.040
How's that?  My X-Saber's blades are sharp!

00:03:45.040 --> 00:03:46.740
I'm not done!

00:03:46.740 --> 00:03:51.580
X-Saber Souza attacks you directly!

00:04:06.490 --> 00:04:09.090
2500 points of damage.

00:04:09.090 --> 00:04:10.230
He withstood it.

00:04:11.190 --> 00:04:12.740
That fires me up!

00:04:12.740 --> 00:04:18.440
That's why he's the successor to You 
Show School's rival Gongenzaka Dojo!

00:04:19.040 --> 00:04:20.840
What are you talking about?

00:04:20.840 --> 00:04:24.080
I set one card and end my turn.

00:04:24.080 --> 00:04:27.090
My turn!  I draw!

00:04:29.690 --> 00:04:33.020
I drew the cornerstone for 
my Immovable Duel style.

00:04:33.640 --> 00:04:41.190
When you have two or more monsters, I can 
Special Summon Superheavy Samurai Scales!

00:04:45.940 --> 00:04:52.670
When this monster is Special Summoned, I can 
Special Summon one Superheavy Samurai from my graveyard!

00:04:53.090 --> 00:04:56.390
Resurrect, Superheavy Samurai Kabuto!

00:04:57.590 --> 00:05:00.280
Not moving is the same as being a mountain.

00:05:00.280 --> 00:05:02.990
I'll show you what immovable means!

00:05:02.990 --> 00:05:09.040
I tribute Superheavy Samurai Scales and Kabuto 
to Tribute Summon a monster in defense position!

00:05:14.590 --> 00:05:18.940
Level 8 Superheavy Samurai Big Benkei!

00:05:19.430 --> 00:05:22.490
Summon a monster faceup in defense position?

00:05:22.490 --> 00:05:26.940
When you summon a monster in defense 
position, it's usually facedown.

00:05:26.940 --> 00:05:33.640
One of Big Benkei's powers is that it can be 
Tribute Summoned faceup in defense position.

00:05:34.440 --> 00:05:37.390
But what's the point?

00:05:37.390 --> 00:05:39.540
I will win without moving!

00:05:40.040 --> 00:05:44.790
This is the soul of Gongenzaka 
Dojo's Immovable Duel style.

00:05:44.790 --> 00:05:46.240
Let's battle!

00:05:46.240 --> 00:05:50.590
Big Benkei attacks XX-Saber Gottoms!

00:05:50.590 --> 00:05:53.340
Attack while it's in defense position?

00:05:53.340 --> 00:05:56.400
Big Benkei is allowed to attack 
while in defense position!

00:06:01.940 --> 00:06:06.410
And its defense points are 
used as its attack points!

00:06:06.410 --> 00:06:07.790
That means...

00:06:07.790 --> 00:06:10.180
It's 3500 vs 3100.

00:06:10.350 --> 00:06:12.820
Big Benkei wins!

00:06:12.820 --> 00:06:15.440
That gives me shivers!

00:06:18.590 --> 00:06:19.890
Good.

00:06:20.360 --> 00:06:22.690
My battle formation is in order.

00:06:22.990 --> 00:06:25.300
I end my turn.

00:06:25.690 --> 00:06:27.840
My turn!  I draw!

00:06:28.640 --> 00:06:33.270
I summon XX-Saber Boggart 
Knight from my hand.

00:06:37.240 --> 00:06:44.440
When Boggart Knight is summoned, I can Special 
Summon one Level 4-or-below X-Saber from my hand!

00:06:44.440 --> 00:06:47.990
Appear, XX-Saber Ragigura!

00:06:48.740 --> 00:06:53.190
Whatever.  It's a weak monster 
with only 200 attack points.

00:06:53.190 --> 00:06:59.600
When Ragigura is Special Summoned, I can 
add one X-Saber in my graveyard to my hand.

00:06:59.840 --> 00:07:02.570
I return Faultroll to my hand.

00:07:02.990 --> 00:07:09.010
I can Special Summon Faultroll when there 
are two or more X-Sabers on my field!

00:07:13.290 --> 00:07:15.540
Faultroll's effect activates!

00:07:15.540 --> 00:07:21.450
Once per turn, I can Special Summon one 
Level 4-or-below X-Saber from my graveyard.

00:07:22.390 --> 00:07:24.540
Another Special Summon?

00:07:24.540 --> 00:07:26.790
He's playing all by himself!

00:07:27.290 --> 00:07:33.630
Resurrect, Tuner Monster 
XX-Saber Fulhelmknight!

00:07:35.090 --> 00:07:37.600
Does this mean...

00:07:37.600 --> 00:07:38.990
That's right!

00:07:38.990 --> 00:07:43.940
Level 3 Fulhelmknight 
tunes Level 6 Faultroll!

00:07:44.840 --> 00:07:47.280
The silver armor shines!

00:07:47.440 --> 00:07:50.240
Crush the hopes of the opposition!

00:07:51.250 --> 00:07:53.140
Synchro Summon!

00:07:53.140 --> 00:07:57.360
Come out, Level 9 XX-Saber Gottoms!

00:08:00.460 --> 00:08:03.840
Oh no.  Just when he destroyed Gottoms...

00:08:03.840 --> 00:08:06.940
Gottoms has 3100 attack points.

00:08:06.940 --> 00:08:09.260
It's no match for Big Benkei!

00:08:09.260 --> 00:08:11.270
That's true!

00:08:12.690 --> 00:08:15.240
But it depends on this.

00:08:15.740 --> 00:08:19.080
All right!  I got the perfect card!

00:08:19.440 --> 00:08:23.440
I activate the Action Spell Extreme Sword!

00:08:24.490 --> 00:08:30.720
Extreme Sword increases a monster's 
attack points by 1000 during battle.

00:08:32.440 --> 00:08:35.290
This is what makes Action Duels thrilling.

00:08:35.290 --> 00:08:39.330
Let's battle!  Gottoms attacks Big Benkei!

00:08:39.490 --> 00:08:41.940
Crush it!

00:08:47.310 --> 00:08:49.090
Big Benkei!

00:08:49.090 --> 00:08:52.390
Even though it's destroyed, he won't take 
damage because it was in defense position.

00:08:52.390 --> 00:08:53.740
That's wishful thinking!

00:08:54.240 --> 00:08:57.290
I activate the trap Meteorain!

00:08:57.890 --> 00:09:05.790
When I attack a monster in defense position this turn, you 
take piercing damage equal to the difference in their points.

00:09:07.040 --> 00:09:10.530
You take 600 points of damage!

00:09:23.180 --> 00:09:25.110
Why?

00:09:25.110 --> 00:09:32.790
When Big Benkei was attacked, I sent Superheavy 
Samurai Soulfire Suit from my hand to the graveyard.

00:09:32.790 --> 00:09:40.940
By sending it to the graveyard, a Level 
5-or-above Superheavy Samurai isn't destroyed this turn!

00:09:42.890 --> 00:09:45.900
You sacrificed your hand to protect your ace.

00:09:46.140 --> 00:09:52.940
But when I use this effect to negate its 
destruction, my monster loses 800 defense points.

00:09:52.940 --> 00:09:55.590
Its defense points went down!

00:09:55.590 --> 00:09:58.990
It's fine.  It's still higher 
than Souza's attack points.

00:09:58.990 --> 00:10:01.950
But what if I get this?

00:10:03.720 --> 00:10:05.180
An Action Card!

00:10:05.500 --> 00:10:08.370
It fell near him!

00:10:08.370 --> 00:10:09.740
If Gongenzaka grabs it...

00:10:09.740 --> 00:10:11.590
Run, Gongenzaka!

00:10:11.590 --> 00:10:13.340
I won't move.

00:10:14.390 --> 00:10:16.740
In that case, I'll take it!

00:10:18.790 --> 00:10:20.340
He got it instead!

00:10:21.340 --> 00:10:24.390
Luck is on my side today!

00:10:24.390 --> 00:10:28.390
I activate the Action 
Spell Extreme Sword again!

00:10:28.390 --> 00:10:31.340
Souza gains 1000 attack points!

00:10:32.240 --> 00:10:35.710
Souza attacks Big Benkei!

00:10:42.190 --> 00:10:47.040
Due to Soulfire Suit's effect, 
Big Benkei isn't destroyed!

00:10:47.040 --> 00:10:50.930
But you still take damage 
due to Meteorain's effect.

00:10:51.090 --> 00:10:52.900
This time, it's 800 points.

00:11:00.640 --> 00:11:02.140
Gongenzaka...

00:11:02.140 --> 00:11:09.190
When Soulfire Suit's effect prevents your 
monster's destruction, your monster loses 800 defense points.

00:11:09.650 --> 00:11:16.640
Yeah, but Gottoms and Souza's attack points 
return to normal at the end of battle.

00:11:17.940 --> 00:11:22.390
You used the effects of the monsters 
in your hand to barely survive.

00:11:22.390 --> 00:11:25.640
For a big guy, you use 
little annoying techniques.

00:11:25.640 --> 00:11:30.670
I believe in my deck, and my deck saved me!

00:11:31.340 --> 00:11:33.840
Time to put an end to your insolence!

00:11:33.840 --> 00:11:37.740
I tribute Boggart Knight to 
activate Gottoms's effect.

00:11:37.740 --> 00:11:40.990
One card in your hand is 
sent to the graveyard.

00:11:41.590 --> 00:11:42.640
What?

00:11:43.990 --> 00:11:46.340
Gongenzaka's hand!

00:11:48.320 --> 00:11:50.690
I'll make you discard your last card too!

00:11:51.740 --> 00:11:56.760
I tribute Ragigura to activate 
Gottoms's effect again!

00:11:59.740 --> 00:12:01.940
His final card!

00:12:04.040 --> 00:12:06.540
You have zero cards in your hand.

00:12:06.540 --> 00:12:09.010
You can't do anything.

00:12:09.190 --> 00:12:12.690
I set one card and end my turn.

00:12:12.980 --> 00:12:14.440
Oh no!

00:12:14.440 --> 00:12:17.590
If nothing changes, Gongenzaka 
will definitely lose!

00:12:17.590 --> 00:12:20.240
If he only took that Action Card.

00:12:20.240 --> 00:12:23.240
Exactly!  Why didn't he take the Action Card?

00:12:23.240 --> 00:12:25.440
It's so strange that it gives me shivers!

00:12:25.440 --> 00:12:27.190
No, it's fine.

00:12:28.240 --> 00:12:30.490
This is his dueling style.

00:12:33.190 --> 00:12:37.540
In a duel, you have to 
believe in your own deck.

00:12:37.540 --> 00:12:43.690
You don't know what Action Card you'll get, so 
putting your hopes in them puts you at a disadvantage.

00:12:44.440 --> 00:12:47.740
But not knowing what you'll 
get is more exciting!

00:12:47.740 --> 00:12:51.940
Besides, how are you going 
to battle with this deck?

00:12:52.390 --> 00:12:55.890
This is the perfect deck for 
Gongenzaka's Immovable Duel style.

00:12:56.390 --> 00:13:01.390
I believe in my deck and promise to win!

00:13:04.640 --> 00:13:06.000
Gongenzaka...

00:13:06.590 --> 00:13:10.790
You believe in your Immovable 
Duel, so use it to win!

00:13:16.580 --> 00:13:19.240
My turn!  I draw!

00:13:21.340 --> 00:13:26.440
I summon Superheavy Samurai 
Soulshield Wall from my hand!

00:13:26.440 --> 00:13:32.240
This monster equips on to a Superheavy 
Samurai and increases its defense points by 1200.

00:13:36.490 --> 00:13:39.490
You drew a monster that 
powers up another monster?

00:13:39.490 --> 00:13:41.490
You're so lucky.

00:13:41.490 --> 00:13:44.840
It wasn't luck that I drew this monster.

00:13:45.190 --> 00:13:47.290
It's because I was prepared!

00:13:47.290 --> 00:13:48.540
Let's battle!

00:13:48.540 --> 00:13:52.680
Big Benkei attacks X-Saber Souza!

00:14:05.760 --> 00:14:07.290
He did it!

00:14:07.290 --> 00:14:08.840
Nice, Gongenzaka!

00:14:09.290 --> 00:14:11.140
How dare you!

00:14:11.140 --> 00:14:13.400
You don't know when to give up!

00:14:13.400 --> 00:14:16.990
I activate the trap Gottoms' Emergency Call!

00:14:16.990 --> 00:14:23.590
When there's an X-Saber on the field, this card 
Special Summons two X-Sabers from the graveyard!

00:14:23.590 --> 00:14:27.890
Resurrect, X-Saber Souza and Ragigura!

00:14:28.590 --> 00:14:33.550
Ragigura's effect returns Faultroll 
from my graveyard to my hand!

00:14:33.790 --> 00:14:38.140
After going through the trouble of 
destroying Souza, he resurrected it right away.

00:14:38.140 --> 00:14:43.340
He also returned Ragigura from the graveyard 
and added Faultroll to his hand!

00:14:43.340 --> 00:14:46.140
It doesn't matter if it's 
the opponent's turn.

00:14:46.140 --> 00:14:48.870
His monsters keep resurrecting.

00:14:49.090 --> 00:14:54.340
This explosive turn of events shows 
why his X-Saber deck is scary.

00:14:54.340 --> 00:14:58.140
It's unusual that you praise 
someone else's deck.

00:14:58.140 --> 00:15:01.140
Is it because you lost?  And you're gutless?

00:15:06.290 --> 00:15:08.790
100 life points and zero cards in his hand.

00:15:08.790 --> 00:15:11.340
There's no way Gon can win.

00:15:11.340 --> 00:15:12.740
No, it's not over.

00:15:13.540 --> 00:15:15.790
He hasn't given up yet.

00:15:21.440 --> 00:15:23.540
My turn.  I draw!

00:15:26.090 --> 00:15:29.190
Do you remember this card?

00:15:29.190 --> 00:15:37.390
XX-Saber Faultroll.  You can Special Summon it 
when you have two or more X-Sabers on your field.

00:15:37.390 --> 00:15:38.390
That's right.

00:15:38.390 --> 00:15:44.290
Since I have at least two X-Sabers on 
my field, I Special Summon Faultroll!

00:15:47.660 --> 00:15:50.680
Next, Faultroll's effect activates!

00:15:50.680 --> 00:15:56.640
Once per turn, I can Special Summon one 
Level 4-or-below X-Saber from my graveyard!

00:15:57.500 --> 00:16:03.840
Resurrect, Tuner Monster 
XX-Saber Fulhelmknight!

00:16:04.290 --> 00:16:08.090
Since he has both Faultroll and 
Fulhelmknight on his field...

00:16:08.090 --> 00:16:14.150
That's right!  Level 3 Fulhelmknight 
tunes Level 6 Faultroll!

00:16:14.790 --> 00:16:19.040
I'll have two Gottoms, which are 
the strongest of the X-Sabers!

00:16:19.040 --> 00:16:20.960
Watch closely!

00:16:21.240 --> 00:16:23.340
Synchro Summon!

00:16:23.340 --> 00:16:27.570
Come out, Level 9 XX-Saber Gottoms!

00:16:33.340 --> 00:16:37.210
I use Souza's effect to tribute Ragigura.

00:16:38.390 --> 00:16:41.390
You're wondering why I did that.

00:16:41.390 --> 00:16:42.840
You'll find out soon enough.

00:16:42.840 --> 00:16:44.140
Let's battle!

00:16:44.140 --> 00:16:46.690
Souza attacks Big Benkei!

00:16:46.890 --> 00:16:50.440
Why?  Souza has fewer attack points!

00:16:50.440 --> 00:16:58.030
By tributing one X-Saber, Souza can destroy 
the monster it's battling this turn.

00:16:58.890 --> 00:17:02.440
Destroy it irregardless of its attack points?

00:17:02.440 --> 00:17:08.390
I'll slice apart your ace monster that 
you're doing everything to protect!

00:17:08.390 --> 00:17:11.010
Soulshield Wall's effect activates!

00:17:11.010 --> 00:17:19.020
By sending it to the graveyard, I can lower my 
previously-equipped monster's defense points to 0 to negate your attack.

00:17:21.670 --> 00:17:22.620
Damn!

00:17:22.870 --> 00:17:28.470
But even if you negate the attack, your monster 
is useless because it lost all its defense points!

00:17:28.470 --> 00:17:32.810
My two Gottoms will annihilate 
it and your life points!

00:17:32.810 --> 00:17:36.590
The first Gottoms attacks Big Benkei!

00:17:36.590 --> 00:17:38.470
I was waiting for that!

00:17:38.470 --> 00:17:43.560
I activate Superheavy Samurai Soulbreaker 
Armor's effect from my graveyard!

00:17:43.560 --> 00:17:46.240
What?  Activate from the graveyard?

00:17:46.240 --> 00:17:48.680
No way!  Is that card...

00:17:48.680 --> 00:17:55.330
It is.  You used Gottoms's effect to send 
this card from my hand to the graveyard.

00:17:55.330 --> 00:17:58.760
This card unleashes its true potential 
when it's in the graveyard.

00:17:58.760 --> 00:18:06.460
By banishing Soulbreaker Armor when there 
are no spell or trap cards in my graveyard...

00:18:06.460 --> 00:18:13.640
...when you attack my monster, you take damage 
equal to the change in my monster's defense points!

00:18:13.640 --> 00:18:15.160
What?

00:18:15.160 --> 00:18:18.640
Big Benkei originally 
had 3500 defense points.

00:18:18.640 --> 00:18:20.470
And it has 0 right now.

00:18:20.470 --> 00:18:23.390
That means it's 3500 points of big damage!

00:18:23.390 --> 00:18:25.900
Gongenzaka wins!

00:18:27.960 --> 00:18:29.210
No way...

00:18:29.840 --> 00:18:35.360
In order to deal this blow, he can't have 
any spell or trap cards in his graveyard.

00:18:35.560 --> 00:18:40.260
That's why Gongenzaka didn't put any 
spell or trap cards in his deck.

00:18:40.260 --> 00:18:42.470
It only contains monsters.

00:18:43.840 --> 00:18:46.990
A deck that only contains monsters?

00:18:46.990 --> 00:18:49.040
That's crazy!

00:18:49.040 --> 00:18:50.530
I see.

00:18:50.530 --> 00:18:54.350
That's why you didn't take any Action Cards.

00:18:54.590 --> 00:18:55.790
That's right.

00:18:55.790 --> 00:18:58.550
Because Action Cards are also spell cards.

00:18:58.550 --> 00:19:02.390
See?  This is the essence 
of Immovable Dueling!

00:19:04.720 --> 00:19:07.560
How amusing.

00:19:07.560 --> 00:19:11.460
I activiate the Quick-Play Spell 
Saber Reflection from my hand!

00:19:11.460 --> 00:19:15.690
When there's a X-Saber on the 
field, effect damage is negated!

00:19:15.690 --> 00:19:17.500
He still had a counter strategy?

00:19:17.690 --> 00:19:21.840
And you take the damage that was negated!

00:19:21.840 --> 00:19:24.290
This is the end!

00:19:27.090 --> 00:19:28.590
I will not fail!

00:19:29.150 --> 00:19:34.090
I activate Superheavy Samurai Soulbang 
Cannon's effect from the graveyard!

00:19:34.090 --> 00:19:36.890
That's another card I sent to the graveyard!

00:19:36.890 --> 00:19:46.770
When there are no spell or trap cards in my graveyard, I 
can banish this card to negate your card effect's damage!

00:19:47.190 --> 00:19:50.340
The damage that I reflected back is negated!

00:19:50.340 --> 00:19:51.740
That's not all!

00:19:51.740 --> 00:20:01.180
All our monsters are destroyed, and we both take 
damage equal to their total Level multiplied by 100 points!

00:20:01.590 --> 00:20:02.790
What?

00:20:02.790 --> 00:20:05.580
The total Level is 33.

00:20:05.580 --> 00:20:08.390
3300 points of damage!

00:20:31.390 --> 00:20:33.090
So this is...

00:20:33.090 --> 00:20:34.540
A draw?

00:20:38.140 --> 00:20:39.740
Gongenzaka!

00:20:40.290 --> 00:20:41.540
Are you okay?

00:20:41.540 --> 00:20:42.790
Pull yourself together.

00:20:43.490 --> 00:20:45.040
I'm sorry.

00:20:45.040 --> 00:20:51.460
My Gongenzaka Immovable Duel 
style wasn't able to defeat him.

00:20:51.460 --> 00:20:53.540
What are you talking about?

00:20:53.540 --> 00:20:56.890
Only you could've pulled 
off a draw, Gongenzaka.

00:20:56.890 --> 00:21:01.140
You believed in your deck, 
and I witnessed its power.

00:21:01.740 --> 00:21:06.580
After three matches, it's 
1 win, 1 loss, 1 draw.

00:21:06.580 --> 00:21:12.390
Chairwoman Akaba, you said that you would take 
this school if you won the three-match contest.

00:21:12.390 --> 00:21:17.390
But it's a draw, so please leave.

00:21:17.740 --> 00:21:19.890
What are you talking about?

00:21:19.890 --> 00:21:22.540
This duel must settle matters.

00:21:22.540 --> 00:21:24.530
There is no such thing as a draw!

00:21:24.690 --> 00:21:28.940
But the duel ended in a draw.

00:21:28.940 --> 00:21:30.840
We'll have overtime!

00:21:30.840 --> 00:21:33.890
The two winners will duel each other.

00:21:33.890 --> 00:21:35.040
Okay?

00:21:35.290 --> 00:21:37.490
You can't do whatever you like!

00:21:43.990 --> 00:21:45.320
Yuya...

00:21:45.740 --> 00:21:48.340
Looks like you want to battle.

00:21:48.340 --> 00:21:49.890
In that case...

00:21:50.340 --> 00:21:51.290
Wait.

00:21:56.890 --> 00:21:59.030
I'll face him.

00:22:12.460 --> 00:22:17.940
Catch the dream dancing in my heart
Release my falling tears

00:22:18.160 --> 00:22:27.420
I'll step out on to my first field
To meet my miracle  Fabulous One Step

00:22:34.310 --> 00:22:39.430
I realized that strength can't be given

00:22:39.690 --> 00:22:44.670
It's something I have to grab myself

00:22:44.960 --> 00:22:50.110
In that case, I have to keep moving
I can't stay still

00:22:50.360 --> 00:22:55.370
Even if walls and headwinds block my way

00:22:55.570 --> 00:23:00.970
I'll draw my trump card called 
"courage" to take a step forward

00:23:00.970 --> 00:23:05.390
I believe in my story of victory

00:23:05.680 --> 00:23:11.360
Everyone during battle is My Way
Duelists are being tested

00:23:11.360 --> 00:23:16.770
When times are tough, that's when you 
Smile, Jump, Fight & Step Up!

00:23:16.770 --> 00:23:22.070
Your smile is your Energy
Kick away your feelings of running away

00:23:22.070 --> 00:23:31.440
Jump into the new field
Shiny One Step that leads to the future

00:23:32.440 --> 00:23:39.660
One step... Just one step is fine
That's your Big Chance!!

00:23:45.490 --> 00:23:52.940
He activated four Contracts, so he'll take 
4000 points of damage during his next Standby Phase.

00:23:52.940 --> 00:23:56.650
If Yuya ends his turn, his 
opponent will have 0 life points!

00:23:56.650 --> 00:23:59.040
So Yuya wins?

00:23:59.040 --> 00:24:00.740
That was quick.

00:24:00.740 --> 00:24:04.990
But I don't think he would 
make such a strategic mistake.

00:24:05.740 --> 00:24:10.490
Next time on Yu-Gi-Oh! ARC-V:
D/D/D  Different Dimension Kings

00:24:10.490 --> 00:24:12.940
The fun is only getting started!
